Hi Dave,

I fuzz filesystem images with syzkaller on Linux 7.2-rc5 (KASAN, QEMU
x86-64) and hit a slab-use-after-free in the JFS inode reader.  The reader
touches the block map (bmap) that dbMount() allocates at mount time, i.e.
mount-time structures are read after they have been freed.

The crash
---------

==================================================================
BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in diRead+0xa30/0xc40
Read of size 4 at addr ff11000000144034 by task syz.7.6792/81626

CPU: 0 UID: 0 PID: 81626 Comm: syz.7.6792 Not tainted 7.2.0-rc5 #1 PREEMPT(full)
Hardware name: QEMU Ubuntu 24.04 PC (i440FX + PIIX, 1996), BIOS 1.16.3-debian-1.16.3-2 04/01/2014
